    "According to you, how can LLMs be used to innovate math learning in schools and universities?": "LLMs could personalize explanations by breaking down complex topics (e.g., calculus) into digestible steps for students like me. They’d also adapt quizzes dynamically based on confidence levels, reducing anxiety. For example, they could generate interactive problems or explain mistakes with analogies. My high conscientiousness would appreciate structured feedback, while my low openness might need more engaging formats (e.g., video responses)."
